WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.709 --> 00:00:05.790
When the announcement came that the majority
of Conservative lawmakers DO have confidence

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:10.840
in Theresa May, her supporters could breathe
a sigh of relief.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:15.560
But not everyone could share the joy.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:19.069
About one third of may's own party voted against
her.

00:00:19.069 --> 00:00:21.829
The prime minister's critics think she should
resign.

00:00:21.829 --> 00:00:35.120
She cannot get her deal through....having
failed in her main policy, it would be constitutionally

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:38.260
normal for her to retire from the fray.

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:43.289
After weeks of speculation about how much
support May had from within the party, enough

00:00:43.289 --> 00:00:48.179
letters were sent in to trigger a confidence
vote on her leadership.

00:00:48.179 --> 00:00:52.249
Some conservative politicians are unhappy
with the Brexit deal she's struck with the

00:00:52.249 --> 00:00:54.109
European Union.

00:00:54.109 --> 00:00:58.440
But May warned that ousting her would only
delay or even stop progress.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:03.859
But now that May has survived the vote she
is adamant that she will continue her mission.

00:01:03.859 --> 00:01:08.280
We now need to get on with the job of delivering
Brexit for the British people and building

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:13.840
a better future for this country
Opposition politicians remain unconvinced

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:17.890
that Theresa May's Conservative government
is fit to cope.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:24.530
This is the furthest stage in the Tory party
convulsing and arguing and bringing the bitterness

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:26.960
to the surface over the question of Europe.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:33.950
It’s their problem, but it does impact upon
the nation at an absolutely crucial time of

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:34.950
crisis.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:39.049
May's political survival can't stop the Brexit
clock ticking.

00:01:39.049 --> 00:02:51.560
It's less than four months until the UK is
supposed

00:02:51.560 --> 00:03:25.680
to 
leave

00:03:25.680 --> 00:08:17.990
the EU.

